{"id":"e00t2","name":"Monthly Customer Retention","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>An online shop wants to follow how many customers come back from one month to the next.</p>\n<p>You have the table <b>orders</b>, which describes every order. It has the following columns:</p>\n<ul><li><code>order_id</code> - the ID of the order;</li><li><code>customer_id</code> - the ID of the customer;</li><li><code>ordered_on</code> - the date of the order;</li><li><code>amount</code> - the amount of the order.</li></ul>\n<p>A customer is <b>active</b> in a month if they placed at least one order during that calendar month. A customer is <b>returning</b> in a month if they are active in that month <b>and</b> in the previous calendar month.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row for every month that has at least one order, with:</p>\n<ol><li><code>month</code> - the first day of the month (date);</li><li><code>active</code> - the number of active customers;</li><li><code>returning</code> - the number of returning customers;</li><li><code>retention_pct</code> - <code>returning</code> divided by the number of active customers of the previous calendar month, in percent, rounded to 1 decimal. It is null when the previous calendar month has no active customer.</li></ol>\n<p>Sort by <code>month</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>orders</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>ordered_on</th><th>amount</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2026-01-05</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>2026-01-20</td><td>35</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>2026-01-25</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>2026-02-02</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3</td><td>2026-02-14</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3</td><td>2026-04-01</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2</td><td>2026-04-30</td><td>40</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>month</th><th>active</th><th>returning</th><th>retention_pct</th></tr><tr><td>2026-01-01</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>2026-02-01</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>50.0</td></tr><tr><td>2026-04-01</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>null</td></tr></table></div>\n<p>March has no order, so in April <code>retention_pct</code> is null, and no customer is returning.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["date_trunc","LAG","division entière","NULLIF"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"orders":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["ordered_on","DATE"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-01-05",20],[2,2,"2026-01-20",35],[3,1,"2026-01-25",10],[4,1,"2026-02-02",50],[5,3,"2026-02-14",12],[6,3,"2026-04-01",8],[7,2,"2026-04-30",40]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["month","active","returning","retention_pct"],"rows":[["2026-01-01",2,0,null],["2026-02-01",2,1,50.0],["2026-04-01",2,0,null]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"orders":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["ordered_on","DATE"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[1,7,"2026-12-31",5],[2,7,"2027-01-01",5],[3,8,"2027-01-02",5]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["month","active","returning","retention_pct"],"rows":[["2026-12-01",1,0,null],["2027-01-01",2,1,100.0]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}